\ ==== amb ====

\ Committed amb ( xt1 xt2 -- ): run xt1; if it fails (explicit fail or a unify
\ mismatch) roll back its bindings and run xt2.  Once a branch succeeds the
\ choice is committed -- a later failure does NOT reopen it.  ~ is unify, ? deref.

\ === first branch succeeds: commits, branch 2 never runs ===
[: 1 :] [: 2 :] amb . cr                          \ 1
[: 11 . :] [: 99 . :] amb cr                      \ 11   (branch 2 never prints)

\ === a branch may leave a value ===
[: 3 4 + :] [: 0 :] amb . cr                      \ 7

\ === branch 1 fails via explicit fail -> branch 2 runs ===
[: fail :] [: 7 :] amb . cr                       \ 7

\ === branch 1 fails via unify mismatch -> branch 2 runs ===
[: 1 2 ~ :] [: 8 :] amb . cr                      \ 8

\ === trail rollback: branch 1 binds then fails, undone, branch 2 binds ===
: t  | ?X |  X [: v | v 1 ~ drop fail :] curry  X [: v | v 2 ~ drop :] curry  amb  X ? . ;
t cr                                              \ 2

\ === branch 1 succeeds with a binding: it persists ===
: u  | ?X |  X [: v | v 5 ~ drop :] curry  X [: v | v 9 ~ drop :] curry  amb  X ? . ;
u cr                                              \ 5

\ === nested amb in branch 2 (after branch 1 fails) ===
[: fail :] [: [: fail :] [: 3 :] amb :] amb . cr  \ 3

\ === nested amb in branch 1 (inner first branch wins) ===
[: [: 5 :] [: 6 :] amb :] [: 9 :] amb . cr        \ 5

\ === a def's local amb is fresh per call ===
: pick  | ?X n |  X n [: v value | v value ~ drop :] 2curry  X [: v | v 0 ~ drop :] curry  amb  X ? ;
3 pick . cr                                       \ 3
7 pick . cr                                       \ 7

\ === sequential ambs each commit independently ===
[: 1 :] [: 2 :] amb  [: 3 :] [: 4 :] amb  + . cr  \ 4

\ === both branches fail -> top-level error ===
[: fail :] [: fail :] amb                         \ error

\ === commitment boundary: a downstream mismatch does NOT reopen a committed amb ===
: c  | ?X |  X [: v | v 1 ~ drop :] curry  X [: v | v 2 ~ drop :] curry  amb  X 5 ~ ;
c                                                 \ error: X committed to 1, no live amb

clear

\ ==== choose ====

\ choose ( items goal -- ): run goal with each element in turn; commit to the
\ first element for which it succeeds, fail if none do.

\ commits to the first element greater than 3
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] [: | x | x 3 > if x . else fail then :] choose cr

\ a single-element array
[ 9 ] [: | x | x . :] choose cr

\ enumerate every element by printing and failing; an outer amb catches the final fail
[: [ 1 2 3 ] [: | x | x . fail :] choose :] [: 0 . :] amb cr

\ no element succeeds: the whole choose fails into the outer branch
[: [ 1 2 ] [: drop fail :] choose :] [: 42 . :] amb cr

\ an empty array fails
[: [ ] [: . :] choose :] [: "empty" . :] amb cr

clear

\ ==== solutions / take-solutions ====

\ solutions ( items goal -- arr ): goal's value for every element it succeeds
\ on, in order; take-solutions stops collecting at n. Both roll every
\ binding back and leave the stack as they found it.

\ collect where the goal succeeds; a fail skips the element
[ 1 2 3 4 ] [: dup 2 mod if fail then dup * :] solutions . cr          \ [ 4 16 ]

\ unification as the filter: open-record match, project a field
[ { :n 1 :ok :y } { :n 2 :ok :n } { :n 3 :ok :y } ]
[: { :ok :y } ~ :n @ :] solutions . cr                                 \ [ 1 3 ]

\ bindings made while collecting roll back afterward (findall semantics)
lvar to SQ
[ [ 1 :a ] [ 2 :b ] [ 3 :a ] ] [: [ SQ :a ] ~ drop SQ ? :] solutions . cr   \ [ 1 3 ]
SQ ? . cr                                                              \ ?SQ (unbound again)

\ edges: all fail, empty array
[ 1 2 3 ] [: fail :] solutions . cr                                    \ [ ]
[ ] [: dup :] solutions . cr                                           \ [ ]

\ take-solutions: first n, goal not run past n; n of 0, n past the length
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] [: dup * :] 3 take-solutions . cr                        \ [ 1 4 9 ]
[ 1 2 3 ] [: dup * :] 0 take-solutions . cr                            \ [ ]
[ 1 2 3 ] [: dup * :] 99 take-solutions . cr                           \ [ 1 4 9 ]

\ the goal stops running once n are collected
0 to goal-runs
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] [: | x ^goal-runs | ++ goal-runs x :] 2 take-solutions . cr   \ [ 1 2 ]
goal-runs . cr                                                         \ 2

\ the stack is left as found
depth . cr                                                             \ 0

clear
